Appendix H: Power Analysis and Sensitivity

H.1 Sample Size Formula

For a one-sided test of H_0: \theta \le \delta versus H_1: \theta > \delta,

N \approx \frac{\left( z_{\alpha}\sqrt{\psi} + z_\beta \sqrt{\psi - (\delta^* - \delta)^2} \right)^2}{(\delta^* - \delta)^2},
\tag{H.1}

where \psi = p_{01} + p_{10} is the discordance rate and \delta^* is the assumed true effect.

H.2 Sensitivity Analysis

Remark H.1. The discordance rate \psi can range up to 1. The claim that \psi = 0.50 is conservative is false. When no pilot is available, the conservative choice is \psi = 1, not \psi = 0.50. A preregistered sensitivity analysis over \psi \in [0.2, 1.0] is required.

Table H.1 (Sensitivity of N to \psi). For \delta = 0.10, \delta^* = 0.20, \alpha = 0.05, \beta = 0.20:

\psi N
